Registry acceptance fixtures — sources, licences and derivation
=================================================================

Used by tests/test_registry_acceptance.py and tests/test_sodir_acceptance.py.
Retrieved 2026-09-25.

rvig_tabel33.csv
    Rijksdienst voor Identiteitsgegevens (RvIG), BRP Landelijke tabellen,
    Tabel 33 "Gemeententabel", CSV sorted by code:
    https://publicaties.rvig.nl/media/13307/download
    (listed at https://publicaties.rvig.nl/landelijke-tabellen-32-tm-61).
    Licence: CC0 1.0 — RvIG publishes its content under CC0 unless stated
    otherwise (https://www.rvig.nl/copyright).
    Derivation: the downloaded file is UTF-16; this copy is the same content
    re-encoded as UTF-8, otherwise unchanged. Columns: municipality code,
    name, successor code, start, end (YYYYMMDD; empty = open). The codes
    0000, 0997-0999 and 1999 are not municipalities; the tests drop them.

rvig_aantal_gemeenten.csv
    RvIG, "Cijfers: Aantal gemeenten door de jaren heen":
    https://www.rvig.nl/cijfers-aantal-gemeenten-door-de-jaren-heen
    Licence: CC0 1.0 (as above).
    Derivation: the per-year series (1900-2026) extracted from the page's
    embedded chart data; read as the count on 1 January of each year.

cbs_gebieden_2009.csv
    Source: Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek (CBS), StatLine table 72014ned
    "Gebieden in Nederland 2009", via the OData v3 API
    (https://opendata.cbs.nl/ODataApi/odata/72014ned/).
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ — attribution: CBS.
    Changes: reduced to two columns — the municipality code (RegioS) and the
    province name (the "Provincies" group's Naam column) — with the table's
    fixed-width padding stripped, sorted by code. Produced by
    reduce_cbs_gebieden_2009.py in this directory from the table's
    TypedDataSet JSON.

sodir/
    Synthetic. The files follow the column layout of the Norwegian Offshore
    Directorate's (Sodir) field and production-licence history tables
    (field_operator_hst, field_licensee_hst, licence, licence_licensee_hst),
    and the five field names and licence number are those of real fields,
    but every company, share and date is invented. The fixture was built
    synthetic because no licence statement for the Sodir data was found with
    the local copy of the data. It is written by sodir/build_sodir_synthetic.py
    so that its answers have the shape of the real tables' answers (partner
    counts 4/1/4/4/2 at 2009-06-30, and 18/11/18/20/19 when two of the three
    hops are left undated).
